  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the key uncertainty is whether a simple RNA-only model is already strong and whether multimodal fusion is needed at all. config_026 tests a minimal, strong RNA baseline using scGPT with a single profile and no aggregation or fusion. This will establish a reference for RNA performance and enable a direct follow-up comparison with config_001, which keeps the same RNA encoder and profile setting while adding a ResNet50 image branch and concat fusion, thereby isolating the contribution of image information. This is a budget-efficient first step because it avoids assuming multimodal complexity is necessary and sets up a clean comparison of an important design choice."
}

